son":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99066","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99066","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99066.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99066.patch","merged_at":"2024-11-13T14:39:16Z"},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99043.\r\n\r\nSharing a single mutex for the barriers vector that is used before the start of each frame led into a possible deadlock if during the process of acquiring a transfer worker, there's no available workers due to a low processor count (or an big queue of threaded buffer/texture loading), so an existing worker must be waited on and flushed. This could lead into a deadlock if the frame was also waiting on said worker to finish processing before going ahead with drawing the frame, as the pool mutex was locked.\r\n\r\nThe fix itself makes sense and should be a pretty safe merge.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99